    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73483" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμηρ-ίδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, mostly in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμηρίδαι, οἱ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Homerids,</i> a family or
			guild of poets in Chios, who claimed descent from Homer, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				14.1.35
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hellanic.
				20
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i> ; of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥαψῳδοί,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>imitators</i> or <i>admirers of Homer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				599e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				252b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ion</u>
				530d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				10.65
			</span></i>.</div>
